  "lineage": "Emerging around 1999-2005 across the UK, Netherlands and Germany via Bedrock, Yoshitoshi and later Coldharbour and Pharmacy, tech trance welded techno's rolling, dry drum programming to trance's 138-142 BPM arpeggios — codified by Marco V, Sander van Doorn, Simon Patterson and John Askew with pumping sidechained basslines, minor-key rolling 16th sequences, minimal breakdowns and almost no vocal presence.",
